---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Get started — KC Chat for Cursor"
  description="Install the KC Chat extension, activate your license, and run your first multi-agent workflow in Cursor — in about five minutes."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container tutorial">
      <header class="hero">
        <p class="eyebrow">Get started · 5-minute setup</p>
        <h1>From license to a multi-agent dev team in 5 minutes</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          KC Chat is a Cursor extension that turns a single chat into a team of <strong>specialized AI
          agents</strong> — architect, frontend, backend, QA — running in parallel, with an autopilot
          orchestrator and a live KC Flow progress tracker. You bring your own Cursor account; KC Chat adds
          the orchestration layer on top.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Pricing snapshot -->
      <div class="price-strip">
        <div class="price-pill"><span class="t">Monthly</span><span class="p">$98</span><span class="d">30 days</span></div>
        <div class="price-pill recommend"><span class="t">Yearly</span><span class="p">$198</span><span class="d">365 days · best value</span></div>
        <div class="price-pill"><span class="t">Lifetime</span><span class="p">$298</span><span class="d">100 years</span></div>
        <a class="btn-secondary" href="/pricing">See pricing →</a>
      </div>

      <!-- TOC -->
      <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
        <h2>Contents</h2>
        <ol>
          <li><a href="#what">What KC Chat is</a></li>
          <li><a href="#prereq">Prerequisites</a></li>
          <li><a href="#buy">Buy a license</a></li>
          <li><a href="#install">Install the extension</a></li>
          <li><a href="#activate">Activate your license</a></li>
          <li><a href="#use">Run your first task</a></li>
          <li><a href="#faq">FAQ</a></li>
          <li><a href="#support">Support</a></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <!-- 1. What -->
      <article id="what" class="block">
        <h2>🧭 What KC Chat is</h2>
        <p>
          KC Chat is a productivity layer for Cursor. Instead of one chat doing one task at a time, you run
          several role-specialized agents at once and let an autopilot coordinate them while KC Flow shows you
          exactly what each one is doing.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Multi-agent panel</strong> — spin up architect / frontend / backend / QA agents, each in its own session.</li>
          <li><strong>Autopilot</strong> — give a goal, a budget and success criteria; the orchestrator drives the loop.</li>
          <li><strong>KC Flow</strong> — a live stepper showing progress, sub-steps, and where work is stuck.</li>
          <li><strong>Shared memory</strong> — agents hand off context instead of starting from scratch.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="tip">
          <strong>What the license unlocks:</strong>
          <p>
            The card-key unlocks KC Chat's orchestration features inside the extension. It does <strong>not</strong>
            change how Cursor bills you — you keep using your own Cursor account, plan and model access exactly
            as before. KC Chat sits on top of Cursor, it does not replace or modify Cursor's billing.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- 2. Prerequisites -->
      <article id="prereq" class="block">
        <h2>🛠️ Prerequisites</h2>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>✅ <strong>Cursor IDE</strong> installed, signed in with your own account (any current version).</li>
          <li>✅ <strong>An active Cursor plan</strong> appropriate to your usage — KC Chat uses your normal Cursor model access.</li>
          <li>✅ <strong>Node.js 18+</strong> — the KC Chat MCP server runs locally alongside the extension.</li>
          <li>✅ <strong>A KC Chat license key</strong> shaped like <code>KC-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX</code> (see “Buy a license”).</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <!-- 3. Buy -->
      <article id="buy" class="block">
        <h2>💳 Buy a license</h2>
        <p>Three tiers — all one-time payments, one license = one device:</p>
        <div class="tier-grid">
          <div class="tier-card">
            <div class="tier-badge">Monthly</div>
            <div class="tier-price">$98</div>
            <div class="tier-days">30 days</div>
            <p class="tier-desc">Try it out · single project</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tier-card tier-recommend">
            <div class="tier-badge">Yearly</div>
            <div class="tier-price">$198</div>
            <div class="tier-days">365 days</div>
            <p class="tier-desc">Best value for daily drivers</p>
            <span class="ribbon">Best value</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tier-card">
            <div class="tier-badge">Lifetime</div>
            <div class="tier-price">$298</div>
            <div class="tier-days">100 years</div>
            <p class="tier-desc">Buy once, keep the orchestration tools</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p>
          Checkout is handled by Lemon Squeezy (our merchant of record). After payment we email you a card code
          shaped like <code>KC-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX</code> — keep it somewhere safe; it's your license key.
        </p>
        <p><a class="btn-primary" href="/pricing">Go to pricing →</a></p>
      </article>

      <!-- 4. Install -->
      <article id="install" class="block">
        <h2>📦 Install the extension</h2>

        <h3>4.1 From the Cursor Marketplace (recommended)</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>Open Cursor → <strong>Extensions</strong> (sidebar).</li>
          <li>Search <strong>“KC Chat”</strong>.</li>
          <li>Click <strong>Install</strong>, then reload Cursor when prompted.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3>4.2 From the command line</h3>
        <pre class="cmd">cursor --install-extension kc.kc-chat-panel</pre>
        <p>Then restart Cursor.</p>

        <h3>4.3 Manual install from VSIX</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>Download the <code>kc.kc-chat-panel-X.Y.Z.vsix</code> from <a href="#support">support</a> or your account.</li>
          <li>Cursor → Extensions → top-right <code>···</code> → <em>Install from VSIX…</em></li>
          <li>Select the file and restart Cursor.</li>
        </ol>
      </article>

      <!-- 5. Activate -->
      <article id="activate" class="block">
        <h2>🔑 Activate your license</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Open the <strong>KC Chat panel</strong> in Cursor → <strong>Settings → Activation</strong>.</li>
          <li>Paste your card code <code>KC-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX</code> and click <strong>Activate</strong>.</li>
          <li>
            On first activation the license binds to this device and the extension stores a signed license token
            locally. (You can also activate from <a href="/activate">the activation page</a>.)
          </li>
          <li>The panel shows <em>Activated · expires YYYY-MM-DD</em>. You're ready to go.</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="hint">
          One card = one device. Switching machines? See the FAQ on transfers, or email
          <a href="mailto:support@h540.com">support@h540.com</a>.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- 6. Use -->
      <article id="use" class="block">
        <h2>⚡ Run your first task</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>New project:</strong> open the KC Chat panel → create an <em>Architect</em> agent → ask for a plan first.</li>
          <li><strong>Large refactors:</strong> use Group mode with a Leader; worker agents run in parallel.</li>
          <li><strong>Long-running work:</strong> switch on <em>autopilot</em> with a budget and clear success criteria.</li>
          <li><strong>Visibility:</strong> watch KC Flow for live progress and where any agent is blocked.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="tip">
          <strong>Tip:</strong>
          <p>Start with one Architect agent and a single, well-scoped goal. Add worker agents once you're
            comfortable with how hand-offs and KC Flow steps look.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- 7. FAQ -->
      <article id="faq" class="block">
        <h2>❓ FAQ</h2>

        <details>
          <summary>What exactly does the license unlock?</summary>
          <p>KC Chat's orchestration features inside the extension: the multi-agent panel, autopilot, KC Flow
            and shared memory. It's a productivity layer that runs on top of Cursor.</p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Does it bypass Cursor's limits or change my Cursor bill?</summary>
          <p>No. You use your own Cursor account, plan and model access exactly as normal. KC Chat does not modify
            Cursor or change how Cursor bills you — it coordinates agents within your existing Cursor usage.</p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>What if I switch laptops?</summary>
          <p>A license binds to one device on first activation. Email support with proof of purchase and we'll
            unbind it so you can re-activate on the new machine. A cooldown prevents abuse.</p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Does it phone home?</summary>
          <p>After activation the extension validates your license token locally (HMAC); it doesn't need to call
            our backend to keep working. Your coding traffic goes to Cursor's own services as usual.</p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Can two people share a license?</summary>
          <p>No. A card binds to your device on first activation; a second device triggers
            <code>device_mismatch</code>. Buy one license per seat (bulk discounts available — see support).</p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>What's the refund policy?</summary>
          <p>Full refund within 7 days for licenses that haven't been activated yet. Once activated, refunds are
            handled case-by-case.</p>
        </details>
      </article>

      <!-- 8. Support -->
      <article id="support" class="block">
        <h2>🙋 Support</h2>
        <div class="contact-grid">
          <div class="contact-card">
            <div class="ic">✉️</div>
            <div class="contact-title">Email</div>
            <p><a href="mailto:support@h540.com">support@h540.com</a></p>
          </div>
          <div class="contact-card">
            <div class="ic">📝</div>
            <div class="contact-title">Contact form</div>
            <p><a href="/contact">h540.com/contact</a></p>
          </div>
          <div class="contact-card">
            <div class="ic">📚</div>
            <div class="contact-title">Docs</div>
            <p><a href="/docs">h540.com/docs</a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .tutorial { max-width: 920px; }
    .hero { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
    .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(1.85rem, 4vw, 2.6rem); margin: 0.4rem 0 0.8rem; line-height: 1.2; }
    .eyebrow {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center;
      font-family: var(--font-mono); text-transform: none; font-size: 0.78rem; letter-spacing: 0.01em;
      color: var(--color-accent); font-weight: 500;
    }
    .eyebrow::before { content: '> '; white-space: pre; opacity: 0.55; font-weight: 700; }
    .lead { color: var(--text-secondary); max-width: 42em; margin: 0 auto; line-height: 1.7; }

    .price-strip {
      display: flex; gap: 0.65rem; justify-content: center;
      flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; margin: 0 0 2rem;
    }
    .price-pill {
      background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
      border-radius: 999px; padding: 0.4rem 1rem; display: flex; gap: 0.55rem;
      align-items: baseline; box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
    }
    .price-pill.recommend {
      border-color: var(--color-accent);
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--color-accent-subtle);
    }
    .price-pill .t { font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-primary); }
    .price-pill .p { font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-accent); font-size: 1.05rem; }
    .price-pill .d { font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
    .btn-secondary {
      padding: 0.4rem 0.85rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-accent);
      border-radius: 999px; color: var(--color-accent); font-weight: 600;
      text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.85rem;
    }
    .btn-secondary:hover { background: var(--color-accent-subtle); }

    .toc {
      background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
      border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
      box-shadow: var(--shadow-card); margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }
    .toc h2 { font-size: 0.92rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 0.8rem; }
    .toc ol { margin-left: 1.25rem; line-height: 2; }

    .block {
      background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
      border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 1.75rem 2rem; box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem; scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--header-height) + 1rem);
    }
    .block h2 { font-size: 1.45rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
    .block h3 { font-size: 1.08rem; margin: 1.25rem 0 0.5rem; color: var(--text-primary); }
    .block p { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.75; margin: 0.4rem 0; }
    .block ul, .block ol { margin: 0.6rem 0 0.6rem 1.4rem; line-height: 1.85; color: var(--text-secondary); }
    .block li { margin: 0.18rem 0; }

    code {
      background: var(--color-accent-subtle); color: var(--color-accent);
      padding: 0.05em 0.4em; border-radius: 4px;
      font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.9em;
    }
    .cmd {
      background: var(--bg-code); color: #E2E8F0;
      padding: 0.85rem 1rem; border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
      font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.86rem;
      overflow-x: auto; margin: 0.5rem 0;
    }

    .tip {
      background: #ECFDF5; border-left: 4px solid #10B981;
      padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem; border-radius: var(--radius-sm); margin: 0.6rem 0;
    }
    .tip strong { color: #065F46; }
    .tip p { color: #065F46; margin: 0.3rem 0 0; }

    .checklist { list-style: none; margin-left: 0; }
    .checklist li { padding: 0.25rem 0; }

    .tier-grid {
      display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(190px, 1fr));
      gap: 1rem; margin: 1rem 0;
    }
    .tier-card {
      background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
      border-radius: var(--radius-md); padding: 1.25rem 1rem;
      text-align: center; position: relative;
    }
    .tier-recommend {
      border-color: var(--color-accent);
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--color-accent-subtle);
    }
    .tier-badge { font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-accent); letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase; }
    .tier-price { font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-primary); margin: 0.4rem 0; }
    .tier-days  { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 600; }
    .tier-desc  { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 0.4rem 0 0; }
    .ribbon {
      position: absolute; top: -10px; right: 12px;
      background: var(--color-accent); color: #fff;
      font-size: 0.7rem; padding: 0.15rem 0.6rem; border-radius: 999px; font-weight: 600;
    }

    details {
      background: #F8FAFC; border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
      border-radius: var(--radius-sm); padding: 0.7rem 1rem;
      margin: 0.5rem 0; cursor: pointer;
    }
    details summary {
      font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);
      cursor: pointer; outline: none;
    }
    details[open] summary { color: var(--color-accent); margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
    details p, details ul { color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0.4rem 0; }

    .btn-primary {
      display: inline-block; background: var(--color-accent);
      color: #fff; padding: 0.6rem 1.4rem; border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
      font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 0.5rem;
    }
    .btn-primary:hover { background: var(--color-accent-hover); color: #fff; }

    .hint { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.85rem; }

    .contact-grid {
      display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
      gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1rem;
    }
    .contact-card {
      background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
      border-radius: var(--radius-md); padding: 1rem 1.25rem; text-align: center;
    }
    .contact-card .ic { font-size: 1.6rem; }
    .contact-title { font-weight: 700; margin: 0.4rem 0; }
    .contact-card p { font-size: 0.85rem; margin: 0; }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
